@prompt
# Task: The watering timer

A small text formatter: durations in minutes become text like `45m` or `1h 30m`. One test does not pass. Find and fix the bug.

@hint
In many mode, find the schedule entry whose output looks wrong, then check how format decides between its two branches for that input.

@reference
### Approach (debugging tasks)
1. Read the comment block at the top: what should the output look like?
2. Scroll to the failing test (the ✗). Read what it asserts.
3. Investigate however you like. You can consult the quick reference for a reminder of available probe features.

@hints
short durations show minutes only
very short durations work too
an hour and a half
minutes are padded to two digits
exact hours show zero minutes
a schedule formats every entry
the morning schedule

@code
# Watering Timer #
# Formats a watering duration, given in minutes, as text. #
# Under an hour: "45m". An hour or more: "1h 30m", with    #
# the minutes always two digits.                           #

# Find the failing test (✗) below. #

# Two-digit minutes: 5 becomes "05" #
let pad(n: Int): String =
  if n < 10 then "0" ++ string_of_int(n) else string_of_int(n)
in

let format(minutes: Int): String =
  if minutes > 60
  then string_of_int(minutes / 60) ++ "h " ++ pad(int_mod(minutes, 60)) ++ "m"
  else string_of_int(minutes) ++ "m"
in

# Format a whole watering schedule #
let schedule(times: [Int]): [String] =
  map(times, fun t -> format(t))
in

# ===== TESTS ===== #

hint "short durations show minutes only"
test
  format(45) == "45m"
end;

hint "very short durations work too"
test
  format(5) == "5m"
end;

hint "an hour and a half"
test
  format(90) == "1h 30m"
end;

hint "minutes are padded to two digits"
test
  format(125) == "2h 05m"
end;

hint "exact hours show zero minutes"
test
  format(180) == "3h 00m"
end;

hint "a schedule formats every entry"
test
  schedule([15, 90]) == ["15m", "1h 30m"]
end;

hint "the morning schedule"
test
  schedule([20, 60, 100]) == ["20m", "1h 00m", "1h 40m"]
end

@test
0
